Wow!

2853
02:53:19,660 --> 02:53:20,740
I expected three hundred!

2854
02:53:21,620 --> 02:53:23,580
This is way more than I ever asked for!

2855
02:53:23,740 --> 02:53:24,240
Thank you!

2856
02:53:25,940 --> 02:53:26,480
Incredible.

2857
02:53:27,360 --> 02:53:28,820
I will save your other brothers.

2858
02:53:30,080 --> 02:53:31,160
I'm in it for the money.

2859
02:53:31,160 --> 02:53:33,000
I mean, I'm in it to save the people here.

2860
02:53:34,620 --> 02:53:35,660
I'm in it for that.

2861
02:53:36,360 --> 02:53:37,200
For the good will...

2862
02:53:38,260 --> 02:53:39,320
Of the local...

2863
02:53:39,320 --> 02:53:39,520
Oh!

2864
02:53:40,360 --> 02:53:41,080
Watch this.

2865
02:53:42,060 --> 02:53:42,780
It's time.

2866
02:53:43,100 --> 02:53:44,820
The moment we've all been waiting for.

2867
02:53:46,360 --> 02:53:46,840
Yeah!

2868
02:53:48,400 --> 02:53:49,340
Nothing in him, though.

2869
02:53:51,420 --> 02:53:52,460
Oh, that's disappointing.

2870
02:53:56,720 --> 02:53:57,080
Really?

2871
02:53:58,340 --> 02:53:58,700
Oh!

2872
02:53:58,860 --> 02:53:59,800
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

2873
02:54:02,020 --> 02:54:03,300
We're gonna chop down this tree!

2874
02:54:14,780 --> 02:54:15,460
Re- Okay.

2875
02:54:16,820 --> 02:54:17,180
Fine.

2876
02:54:23,000 --> 02:54:25,100
Why does this look like a man with a fake beard?

2877
02:54:25,960 --> 02:54:26,960
I mean, who am I to speak?

2878
02:54:27,040 --> 02:54:27,760
I have fake legs.

2879
02:54:29,280 --> 02:54:30,000
Yeah, yeah, shut up.

2880
02:54:32,060 --> 02:54:32,640
Uh, you!

2881
02:54:33,360 --> 02:54:35,160
What is the deal with Lon Lon?

2882
02:54:36,100 --> 02:54:39,320
Ingo took over Lon Lon Ranch and they call it Ingo Ranch nowadays.

2883
02:54:39,320 --> 02:54:39,820
I know.

2884
02:54:40,360 --> 02:54:41,640
I was kicked out of there.

2885
02:54:42,860 --> 02:54:43,900
And look at me now.

2886
02:54:44,360 --> 02:54:45,400
My girl Malon.

2887
02:54:45,520 --> 02:54:46,820
She still works at the ranch.

2888
02:54:47,320 --> 02:54:48,360
I'm worried about her.

2889
02:54:49,060 --> 02:54:49,320
Okay.

2890
02:54:49,480 --> 02:54:49,800
You know what?

2891
02:54:49,840 --> 02:54:51,000
We're going to Lon Lon again.

2892
02:54:51,160 --> 02:54:52,680
I'm losing my mind over this.

2893
02:54:53,780 --> 02:54:57,180
There's gotta be something profoundly simple we have missed.

2894
02:54:58,680 --> 02:55:00,940
It's gotta be that way, you know?

2895
02:55:03,160 --> 02:55:04,660
I just can't see...

2896
02:55:05,340 --> 02:55:06,780
what we're supposed to do there.

2897
02:55:09,400 --> 02:55:10,020
Wait a minute.

2898
02:55:10,320 --> 02:55:12,020
Why didn't I try just riding out the gates?

2899
02:55:12,900 --> 02:55:14,440
Instead of trying to jump the fence.

2900
02:55:16,500 --> 02:55:17,840
Was the gate closed or something?

2901
02:55:17,960 --> 02:55:18,780
I forgot the deal.

2902
02:55:19,820 --> 02:55:20,820
Maybe that's the solution.

2903
02:55:25,880 --> 02:55:26,700
We can do it.

2904
02:55:30,680 --> 02:55:31,360
I believe.

2905
02:55:43,500 --> 02:55:44,480
Oh, that was beautiful.

2906
02:55:45,480 --> 02:55:47,960
I managed to blow my nose while running.

2907
02:55:47,960 --> 02:55:49,440
That was such skill.

2908
02:55:50,200 --> 02:55:50,760
Dextrous.

2909
02:55:53,520 --> 02:55:54,420
Very nice.

2910
02:55:56,280 --> 02:55:58,760
I one-handed my nose blowing there.

2911
02:56:03,830 --> 02:56:04,470
Okay.

2912
02:56:06,990 --> 02:56:08,230
Mother crapper.

2913
02:56:08,430 --> 02:56:09,470
Let's see what we got over here then.

2914
02:56:10,550 --> 02:56:10,950
See?

2915
02:56:11,210 --> 02:56:12,730
The gate is open.

2916
02:56:13,410 --> 02:56:14,310
Nevermind, it's closed.

2917
02:56:16,710 --> 02:56:17,670
Can I break in?

2918
02:56:27,750 --> 02:56:30,010
Okay, so what exactly is going on here?

2919
02:56:30,950 --> 02:56:32,610
Okay, we gotta play a melody, of course.

2920
02:56:34,530 --> 02:56:36,150
This is round, uh, five.

2921
02:56:36,810 --> 02:56:37,850
Take five for this.

2922
02:56:39,250 --> 02:56:40,650
Or six or seven, I don't know.

2923
02:56:47,910 --> 02:56:48,590
That's the one.

2924
02:56:55,220 --> 02:56:55,900
Here we go.

2925
02:56:59,060 --> 02:57:01,160
So, why are we able to shoot the bow?

2926
02:57:01,260 --> 02:57:02,440
This is something we need to investigate.

2927
02:57:03,540 --> 02:57:06,540
Like, this is like a real mechanic here.

2928
02:57:09,340 --> 02:57:10,160
Link, what are you doing?

2929
02:57:22,060 --> 02:57:23,200
The gates are closed.

2930
02:57:26,780 --> 02:57:27,500
Oh my god!

2931
02:57:27,500 --> 02:57:28,340
The head scared me.

2932
02:57:28,380 --> 02:57:29,580
I thought it was someone right in front of me.

2933
02:57:30,200 --> 02:57:31,180
I wish I had more time.

2934
02:57:31,280 --> 02:57:32,840
I hate that I'm limited by time here.

2935
02:57:33,600 --> 02:57:34,580
Oh, we can even canter.

2936
02:57:34,760 --> 02:57:35,180
Look at this.

2937
02:57:35,860 --> 02:57:37,520
Or going backwards, whatever it's called.

2938
02:57:38,940 --> 02:57:41,880
Maybe I'm supposed to put on a show here, and the guy will be impressed.

2939
02:57:44,120 --> 02:57:46,100
I think I gotta make enough jumps here.

2940
02:57:46,480 --> 02:57:48,020
To prove that I'm a worthy rider.

2941
02:57:53,220 --> 02:57:54,820
Okay, give me another shot, coach.

2942
02:57:55,500 --> 02:57:56,460
Put me in the game.

2943
02:58:02,230 --> 02:58:05,530
After the horse comes to a complete stop, press A to dismount.

2944
02:58:07,230 --> 02:58:09,970
Okay, so maybe I need to go to the gate dismount?

2945
02:58:25,200 --> 02:58:25,800
Come on.

2946
02:58:27,180 --> 02:58:28,060
Can I lead you?

2947
02:58:28,200 --> 02:58:28,440
No.

2948
02:58:31,700 --> 02:58:33,820
I'm gonna put this guy next to him over here.

2949
02:58:33,940 --> 02:58:35,740
Maybe he'll be impressed by my ability to tame this horse.

2950
02:58:36,320 --> 02:58:37,740
Uh, how do I get off?

2951
02:58:38,900 --> 02:58:39,560
No, no!

2952
02:58:40,420 --> 02:58:41,200
You're getting better!

2953
02:58:41,700 --> 02:58:42,680
How about a little race with me?

2954
02:58:43,220 --> 02:58:44,840
One lap around the corral with that horse.

2955
02:58:45,600 --> 02:58:45,940
Yes!

2956
02:58:46,540 --> 02:58:47,540
Let's make a little wager.

2957
02:58:47,660 --> 02:58:48,400
Say 50 rupees?

2958
02:58:48,920 --> 02:58:49,280
Yes!

2959
02:58:50,420 --> 02:58:51,560
Wait, I did- okay.

2960
02:58:51,800 --> 02:58:53,080
Well, this is exactly what I wanted.

2961
02:58:56,350 --> 02:58:57,050
Let's go!

2962
02:58:58,730 --> 02:58:59,850
Finally making progress!

2963
02:59:03,070 --> 02:59:03,790
Oh, man.

2964
02:59:05,850 --> 02:59:06,750
Fuck you, Ingo.

2965
02:59:06,910 --> 02:59:07,710
You suck!

2966
02:59:08,710 --> 02:59:09,750
I got no more carrots!

2967
02:59:11,370 --> 02:59:12,670
No, the carrots have been used!

2968
02:59:14,230 --> 02:59:14,970
Carrots are back.

2969
02:59:17,550 --> 02:59:18,070
Carrots!

2970
02:59:18,430 --> 02:59:19,490
He's blocking me!

2971
02:59:21,710 --> 02:59:22,830
He's frontgating me!

2972
02:59:25,170 --> 02:59:26,450
No, no, I win, I win.

2973
02:59:26,510 --> 02:59:26,810
I'm in front.

2974
02:59:30,760 --> 02:59:32,000
Too bad for you!

2975
02:59:32,540 --> 02:59:33,960
I got your 50 rupees!

2976
02:59:34,960 --> 02:59:36,660
God, I want to smash your head in.

2977
02:59:39,870 --> 02:59:42,070
Are you mad because you lost?

2978
02:59:43,010 --> 02:59:45,170
If you're that upset, how about another race?

2979
02:59:46,170 --> 02:59:47,930
Bet 50 and race again?

2980
02:59:49,890 --> 02:59:50,410
Deal!

2981
02:59:51,610 --> 02:59:52,470
What's the matter?

2982
02:59:52,910 --> 02:59:57,310
Don't you even- Oh my- I'll be back.

2983
02:59:57,970 --> 02:59:58,850
I'll be back.

2984
02:59:59,890 --> 03:00:01,650
I will go sell you chickens!

2985
03:00:03,150 --> 03:00:03,670
Thanks!

2986
03:00:04,110 --> 03:00:04,850
See you later.

2987
03:00:06,090 --> 03:00:08,050
I'm just gonna pretend to do it to make him angry.

2988
03:00:09,330 --> 03:00:13,090
Wait, where the- There were jars here!

2989
03:00:13,670 --> 03:00:14,750
With money in them!

2990
03:00:17,490 --> 03:00:18,870
Should we have jars up here?

2991
03:00:20,990 --> 03:00:21,570
Jar me!

2992
03:00:23,830 --> 03:00:24,230
Yes!

2993
03:00:26,090 --> 03:00:27,370
Oh, we're making progress here.

2994
03:00:27,430 --> 03:00:28,250
This actually feels good.

2995
03:00:30,110 --> 03:00:34,270
I tried to get off the horse at the gate, but then I guess I didn't.

2996
03:00:36,010 --> 03:00:37,150
I forgot how to do that.

2997
03:00:37,510 --> 03:00:38,430
But I guess it doesn't matter.

2998
03:00:43,280 --> 03:00:44,020
51, baby.

2999
03:00:45,320 --> 03:00:46,500
This is all I have.

3000
03:00:48,040 --> 03:00:49,140
I'm all in on this.

3001
03:00:54,680 --> 03:00:54,900
Hey!

3002
03:00:55,360 --> 03:00:56,040
Wait a minute!

3003
03:00:57,540 --> 03:00:58,260
Hold up!

3004
03:01:02,650 --> 03:01:03,130
Asshole!

3005
03:01:03,270 --> 03:01:04,150
50 for the race!

3006
03:01:08,190 --> 03:01:08,670
No!

3007
03:01:10,810 --> 03:01:12,030
Who you calling a punk?

3008
03:01:13,710 --> 03:01:16,550
I'm just gonna go back into your bedroom and rob you even more blind.

3009
03:01:18,770 --> 03:01:19,510
Stay mad.

3010
03:01:37,100 --> 03:01:37,540
Yeah!

3011
03:01:42,000 --> 03:01:43,100
60 is all we need.

3012
03:01:44,060 --> 03:01:45,120
It's all I need anyway.

3013
03:01:46,900 --> 03:01:47,560
All right, guys.

3014
03:01:47,740 --> 03:01:48,180
Predictions.

3015
03:01:48,760 --> 03:01:51,540
Am I gonna own this race or I'm gonna get owned?

3016
03:01:52,320 --> 03:01:53,600
I'm gonna tell you right now.

3017
03:01:53,600 --> 03:01:56,900
I was just pretending before when I lost the race.

3018
03:01:57,560 --> 03:01:59,320
I was in control all the time.

3019
03:02:00,920 --> 03:02:01,400
So...

3020
03:02:01,400 --> 03:02:02,580
Or am I just telling you that now?

3021
03:02:02,720 --> 03:02:03,740
Am I gonna win or lose?

3022
03:02:04,060 --> 03:02:05,600
I think I'm gonna win spectacularly.

3023
03:02:07,980 --> 03:02:08,460
Yep.

3024
03:02:11,550 --> 03:02:12,330
Let's do it.

3025
03:02:13,590 --> 03:02:14,330
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

3026
03:02:21,100 --> 03:02:21,880
Here we go.

3027
03:02:24,380 --> 03:02:25,300
Come on, Epona!

3028
03:02:28,000 --> 03:02:29,520
Epona used to be Epony.

3029
03:02:30,400 --> 03:02:31,580
Now it's an e-horse.

3030
03:02:35,980 --> 03:02:37,800
Go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go.

3031
03:02:38,780 --> 03:02:39,960
Come on, Link.

3032
03:02:40,060 --> 03:02:40,520
Let's move it.

3033
03:02:40,680 --> 03:02:41,640
Get him on.

3034
03:02:46,830 --> 03:02:47,270
Yes!

3035
03:02:47,890 --> 03:02:49,070
Bring it on, sister.

3036
03:02:52,420 --> 03:02:53,100
Let's do it.

3037
03:02:55,820 --> 03:02:56,860
Bro, he's blocking me.

3038
03:02:56,960 --> 03:02:57,380
He's cheating!

3039
03:02:57,620 --> 03:02:58,500
He's actually cheating!

3040
03:03:03,870 --> 03:03:04,750
What the...

3041
03:03:09,460 --> 03:03:10,660
Bro, piss off!

3042
03:03:11,180 --> 03:03:11,900
No way!

3043
03:03:15,800 --> 03:03:16,420
He's cheating!

3044
03:03:18,100 --> 03:03:19,160
He's blocking me!

3045
03:03:34,910 --> 03:03:35,510
We're done.

3046
03:03:41,290 --> 03:03:42,030
I'm not mad.

3047
03:03:44,710 --> 03:03:45,370
I'm sick.

3048
03:03:46,090 --> 03:03:47,230
This is why I can't win.

3049
03:03:47,370 --> 03:03:48,290
I am sick right now.

3050
03:03:49,290 --> 03:03:50,170
That's why I lost.

3051
03:03:53,630 --> 03:03:54,070
That's...

3052
03:03:54,070 --> 03:03:54,550
It's the truth.

3053
03:03:57,390 --> 03:03:58,430
It is what it is.

3054
03:03:58,630 --> 03:04:00,930
Sometimes, you know, you're sick, and sometimes you're healthy.

3055
03:04:00,930 --> 03:04:02,190
This was not one of those days.

3056
03:04:05,820 --> 03:04:06,720
I'm just kidding.

3057
03:04:07,380 --> 03:04:08,300
I got owned.

3058
03:04:08,460 --> 03:04:08,860
I got owned.

3059
03:04:08,960 --> 03:04:09,320
It's fine.

3060
03:04:10,000 --> 03:04:11,100
Next time we're gonna get him.

3061
03:04:14,980 --> 03:04:15,740
Oh, man.

3062
03:04:19,420 --> 03:04:21,840
I actually forgot I was sick halfway through this stream.

3063
03:04:22,380 --> 03:04:23,780
That's how good this game is.

3064
03:04:24,140 --> 03:04:25,180
You get immersed.

3065
03:04:28,760 --> 03:04:30,660
Never having faith ever again.

3066
03:04:32,260 --> 03:04:32,740
Listen.

3067
03:04:33,840 --> 03:04:36,420
It's the always darkest just before dawn.

3068
03:04:36,640 --> 03:04:38,380
It's not actually true, but you know the saying, right?

3069
03:04:39,140 --> 03:04:42,160
So next time, definitely all in on my success.

3070
03:04:46,250 --> 03:04:47,770
Horse privileges withdrawn.

3071
03:04:48,130 --> 03:04:49,710
I never had any privileges.

3072
03:04:49,950 --> 03:04:50,990
I paid for those privileges.

3073
03:04:51,410 --> 03:04:52,470
And now I'm poor.

3074
03:04:54,990 --> 03:04:56,310
You love the Zelda streams?

3075
03:04:56,450 --> 03:04:56,650
Thanks.

3076
03:04:57,290 --> 03:04:58,050
I love them too.

3077
03:04:58,810 --> 03:04:59,510
Next two of us.

3078
03:05:05,700 --> 03:05:08,980
I can't listen to this OST without thinking about wanting Talos 2.

3079
03:05:09,080 --> 03:05:10,860
I've actually been thinking about Talos 2 recently.

3080
03:05:12,140 --> 03:05:14,440
But I've also been thinking about Expedition 33.

3081
03:05:15,300 --> 03:05:16,520
And Journey 24.

3082
03:05:17,760 --> 03:05:18,980
And The Trip 19.

3083
03:05:21,300 --> 03:05:22,240
All those games.

3084
03:05:24,400 --> 03:05:25,240
I want to play them.

3085
03:05:34,080 --> 03:05:35,860
I wish you had your breaks in the windmill.

3086
03:05:36,040 --> 03:05:36,740
Oh, you know what?

3087
03:05:36,740 --> 03:05:38,480
That's actually a good idea, but...

3088
03:05:38,480 --> 03:05:42,300
If only there was an easy way to transport back to the windmill.

3089
03:05:42,460 --> 03:05:43,300
Then I would do it.

3090
03:05:45,160 --> 03:05:45,940
Or even better.

3091
03:05:46,440 --> 03:05:48,440
I wish I could make the windmill my home.

3092
03:05:48,880 --> 03:05:52,600
So that when I start the game again, I start in the windmill and not in the middle of, uh...

3093
03:05:53,260 --> 03:05:54,260
You know, pagan hell.

3094
03:06:00,250 --> 03:06:04,110
E33 would be funny for someone that hasn't played Mario 64 in years?

3095
03:06:04,910 --> 03:06:05,430
Really?

3096
03:06:06,730 --> 03:06:08,570
Are those games related at all?

3097
03:06:08,650 --> 03:06:09,570
That doesn't seem like it.

3098
03:06:10,690 --> 03:06:12,350
I mean, I don't know, but...

3099
03:06:12,350 --> 03:06:13,370
I doubt it.

3100
03:06:13,990 --> 03:06:15,150
Maybe you're just joking.

3101
03:06:19,900 --> 03:06:20,700
Thanks, LeeJ.

3102
03:06:23,570 --> 03:06:26,570
You should play Wind Waker after Ocarina of Time.

3103
03:06:27,730 --> 03:06:28,450
We'll see.

3104
03:06:29,510 --> 03:06:31,830
There's also Majora's Mask and stuff, right?

3105
03:06:32,290 --> 03:06:37,170
I guess if I were to choose, I'm probably gonna do it in the release order, whatever that is.

3106
03:06:37,970 --> 03:06:40,630
I don't know what release order is, but I'm gonna do it in that order.

3107
03:06:45,420 --> 03:06:46,100
If anything.

3108
03:06:54,730 --> 03:06:55,750
Majora is the sequel.

3109
03:06:55,930 --> 03:06:56,870
Oh, okay, perfect then.

3110
03:06:57,090 --> 03:06:57,170
Yeah.

3111
03:06:58,850 --> 03:07:01,610
Well, then it makes sense to play that after, uh...

3112
03:07:01,610 --> 03:07:02,930
Or as the next Zelda game.

3113
03:07:06,300 --> 03:07:09,000
I kinda regret playing Breath of the Wild as the first game.

3114
03:07:10,320 --> 03:07:12,740
I think that game would have been more special if I had waited.

3115
03:07:13,960 --> 03:07:15,360
Until I played the originals.

3116
03:07:16,420 --> 03:07:19,180
I guess I just assumed the originals would be kinda bad, you know?

3117
03:07:19,280 --> 03:07:20,080
Like, as in...

3118
03:07:20,500 --> 03:07:21,400
Haven't aged well.

3119
03:07:22,060 --> 03:07:22,960
Boy, was I wrong.

3120
03:07:25,540 --> 03:07:27,400
Imagine if they made a remake...

3121
03:07:28,040 --> 03:07:30,040
Of Ocarina of Time, but in 2025.

3122
03:07:31,160 --> 03:07:32,300
What would that even look like?

3123
03:07:32,320 --> 03:07:34,440
I guess it would look like Breath of the Wild a little bit.

3124
03:07:35,700 --> 03:07:36,060
Yeah.

3125
03:07:36,880 --> 03:07:38,840
But I guess the old style has its charm.

3126
